    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "\"This CD-ROM contains aeromagnetic data obtained between September 1998 and February 1999 over a large area in southern Wisconsin. The survey was flown and the data were processed by High-Sense Geophysics Limited under contract with the U.S. Geological Survey. The total flight distance was about 46,000 line-miles (74,000 km) with traverse lines spaced at one-half mile (805m) and oriented in a north-south direction. The altitude was draped to topography at 1000 feet (305m) above ground level.\"",
